#X text 82 626 0: messages (see Messages below), f 64;
#X obj 60 670 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 694 0: signal left \; 1: signal right \; 2: events: value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 770 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 794 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, routed by ch1 / ch2 \; note2 <p> <v>: a note for line 2 alone (with trk 0) \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. wav1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. trk 0 (see Settings below) \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \, phase: restart all phases \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump cz1 v0 ..' \; dump cz1 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \;   old lines 'dump cz4 ...' from before the rename work too \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly \; tone b0 ... b127: waves \, levels and detune from a CZ-1 tone \; quant \, chiprate \, bits \, dacerr \, hiss \, lpf \, drive: single \; vintage stages instead of era, f 64;
#X obj 60 1094 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1118 0 wav1 (0) Waveform of line 1. Morphs through the CZ waves: \; saw \, saw-pulse \, square \, pulse \, resonance with saw \, triangle \, \; cosine \, trapezoid \, pulse and double-saw window \, double sine \, \; double pulse. \; 1 wav2 (0) Waveform of line 2 \, same range. \; 2 dcw1 (6) DCW of line 1: how far the sine is bent towards the \; waveform (0 = sine). \; 3 dcw2 (6) DCW of line 2. \; 4 detn (0) Detunes line 2 upwards \, continuously: 0 = unison \, \; 127 = one octave up. fine adds +-50 cents. \; 5 amp1 (127) Level of line 1. \; 6 amp2 (0) Level of line 2. With ring: level of the ring \; product. Above full scale (amp1 + amp2 > 127) both are scaled \; down together \, so two lines never clip. \; 7 mod (0) Modulation of line 2: 0-42 off \, 43-85 ring \, 86-127 \; noise., f 64;
#X obj 60 1402 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Settings\ (name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1426 pai1 \, pai2 (-1) second wave of a CZ wave pair 0-11 \, -1 = off \; octv (0) octave -1 \, 0 \, 1 \; sprd (0.5) stereo spread of the 4 voices 0-1 \; levl (0.5) output level 0-2 \; drft (0) slow pitch drift per voice 0-1 \; mrph (8) smoothing of wave changes in ms \; hold (1) released voices keep sounding until the next phrase \; a4 (440) tuning in Hz \; dvel (40) how much velocity adds to the DCW of both lines \; trk (1) 1: line 2 follows line 1 \, 0: line 2 has its own notes \; ch1 (0) MIDI channel of line 1 \, 0 = any \; ch2 (2) MIDI channel of line 2 (with trk 0) \; pmor (1) 1: morph the bent phase \, 0: CZ-style crossfade \; sine (1) 1: DCW 0 = sine on every wave \, 0: chip behaviour \; era (0) vintage character 0-127: chip resolution \, chip rate \, \; DAC and output stage \, from clean to crunchy \; fine (64) fine detune of line 2 \, 64 = none \, +-50 cents \; pat8 (0) 1: resonance through the 8-bit circuit of the patent \; fade (4) voice fade in/out at note-on and note-off \, 1-100 ms\; \; short = snappy CZ attack \, longer = no click with an open VCA, f 64;
#X obj 60 1774 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Wave\ morph 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1798 wav moves through 12 waves. Neighbours are ordered so \; they sound close \, and with pmor 1 the bent phase itself is \; interpolated: one single wave at every point \, no level dip. \; With sine 1 every wave starts from the plain sine at DCW 0 \, \; so a DCW envelope always opens from the same sine. \; pmor 0 and sine 0 give the CZ chip's own behaviour. \; The cosine window (position 6) comes from Casio's patent: a \; resonance without the buzz of the chip's windows. \; pat8 1 sends the resonance waves (positions 4-9) through the \; patent's 8-bit circuit: a 256-step cosine ROM with 8-bit \; values \, an 8-bit window and 8 x 8 bit products - stepped and \; gritty., f 64;
#X obj 60 2018 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Two\ lines 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2042 Every voice has two lines \, each with its own wave and DCW. \; With trk 1 line 2 plays the same notes \, detuned by detn. \; With trk 0 it gets its own 4-voice allocation and notes from \; MIDI channel ch2 \, like a second oscillator: two sequencer \; tracks on one voice \, levelled by amp1 and amp2 \, joined by \; ring or noise. detn and fine tune line 2 against line 1., f 64;
#X obj 60 2166 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Envelopes 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2190 cz1~ has no envelopes. A note-on restarts its voice's phase \, \; velocity opens the DCW (dvel) \, and the level is shaped by an \; external VCA. With hold 1 a released chord keeps sounding \; until the next phrase \, so the VCA's release stays intact., f 64;
#X obj 60 2282 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ steps 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2306 Per-step values: connect the voice to [skpreset name] \; (outlet 2 -> inlet 0 \, outlet 0 -> voice inlet). A slot \; number 0-15 then recalls and keeps the values for a step. \; More in skpreset-help.pd (click to open)., f 64;
